                <pb facs="0520" n="424" sameAs="frus:frus1926v02/pg424"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">438.00/367: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The High Commissioner in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Russell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-01-30T14:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 30,
                                1926—2 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received February 1—9:40
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>11. Department’s 6, January 26, 7 p.m. Minister for Foreign Affairs has verbally
                    informed me that he accepts suggested observations and explanations. At my
                    [suggestion he is] informing Haitian Minister at Washington accordingly.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Russell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
